# 2. CRITICAL RULE — PUBLIC USER VS ADMIN/DEVELOPER

Create a strict separation.

## PUBLIC USER

A normal user must NEVER see:

* backend health check
* API health check
* database connection
* PostgreSQL status
* Qdrant status
* vector count
* embedding status
* Groq status
* model name
* RAG terminology
* retrieval scores
* similarity scores
* chunk counts
* top-K values
* latency
* API endpoints
* raw JSON
* developer errors
* stack traces
* technical IDs
* internal database IDs
* internal document IDs
* internal standard IDs unless they are legitimate BIS identifiers
* SIH references
* problem statement numbers
* phase numbers
* development notes
* prototype labels
* demo labels
* developer tools
* debug information

## ADMIN / INTERNAL

Technical information MAY exist inside an authenticated admin/internal area.

Create or preserve a clearly separated admin area for:

* system health
* knowledge base
* documents
* ingestion
* indexing
* vector database
* AI configuration
* evaluation
* feedback
* logs
* system diagnostics

But these MUST NOT leak into the public product.

